   "code": "CONFOUNDING",
   "text": "The observed effect might be confounded by other variables, such as the initial offensive set, the quality of the PNR ball-handler or screener, the defensive reaction to the drive, or the general offensive efficiency of the team. Without controlling for these, a causal inference is risky."
